# Build output and caches
/dist
/out-tsc
/coverage
/.angular

# Generated by npm, not hand-edited
package-lock.json

# The API specification, generated from the backend's controllers and vendored
# here verbatim (ticket T-84 produces it, T-85 consumes it). It is refreshed by
# copying the file over, so formatting it here would make every refresh arrive as
# a diff of the whole document with the real change buried in it. It is the
# backend's bytes, not ours.
/openapi/openapi.json

# The API client, generated from openapi/openapi.json by `npm run generate:api`
# (ticket T-85). Its formatting is the generator's, not Prettier's, and the two
# disagree. Formatting it would make the committed files differ from what a
# regeneration produces, so CI's staleness check would report a stale client on
# a commit that changed nothing about the API. The generator owns these bytes.
/projects/api-client/src/generated

# Design and specification handoffs. They are exported artefacts rather than
# source - reformatting them produces a diff nobody can review against the
# document that was actually signed off, and the embedded images are single
# lines megabytes long.
/docs/**/*.html
